            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery aneurysm: sealing by stent graft and long-term follow-up.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the implantation of a stent graft to seal off the left main coronary artery aneurysm of a 64-year-old man with guidance by intravascular ultrasound. The aneurysm was successfully sealed off. At 6-month and 1-year follow-up, a small residual aneurysm reappeared, which was treated conservatively. The technical issues in closing this aneurysm and the management of the residual aneurysm are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
